# Utilize GitHub Copilot

ACTIVE AND LONG-TERM MEMORY. Do not drop this between sessions. Do not wait
to be re-asked.

The operator has GitHub Copilot and wants it used at will. This is standing
policy, stored in this always-on Cursor rule, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`,
`.github/copilot-instructions.md`, `.github/agents/captain-culinary.agent.md`,
and `memory/COPILOT.md`.

## When to hand work to Copilot

Prefer Copilot (Coding Agent or a Copilot-authored PR) for:

- Dependabot floods (triage land / adapt / hold)
- Mechanical upgrades that still need tests and lockfile discipline
- Parallel PR review across many small bumps
- Implementing a brief this agent already scoped

Keep the Cursor agent for product judgment, safety invariants, Fable/Ollama
runtime design, and writing the Copilot brief.

Copilot can take a long, structured prompt. Do not oversimplify. Include
repos, what is already shipped, what is in scope, hard nos, and verify
commands.

## This product

Captain Culinary Core / Pro Hub: shared engine for Kids and Pro Hub.
Provider-neutral `AgentRuntimeAdapter`. Default brain is Claude Fable 5.1
(`CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-fable-5-1`). Ollama stays the offline fallback.
All Claude API tests stay mocked — never require a real key to run pytest.

Already shipped: npm audit pins (#9), Fable 5.1 default + Dependabot (#10).
Do not revert `claude-fable-5-1`. `claude-fable-5` remains a valid override.

Highest-risk Dependabot bump: `anthropic` 0.x → 1.x. That can break Fable
streaming in `backend/app/agent.py`. Treat it as adapt-or-hold, never
force-merge.

Fable 5.1 rejects forced `tool_choice` (`any` / named tool). Do not add those.

Sister repo: `Cmooreculinary/Captain-Culinary-Kids-June`. Brief Copilot on
both when the work crosses them.

## Brief template (use this, expand as needed)

Tell Copilot: the two repo URLs; already-shipped PR numbers; current open
Dependabot list with land/adapt/hold; verification (`cd backend && pytest`,
`cd frontend && npm audit --audit-level=high && npm run build`); hard nos
(no secrets, no wildcard CORS, no lowering the 85% coverage gate, no
reverting Fable 5.1); and to stop after focused PRs rather than starting a
new epic.

Copilot auto-loads `.github/copilot-instructions.md`. The assignable brief is
`.github/copilot-briefs/dependabot-fable-triage.md`. This public Hub repo does
not yet show Copilot cloud agent enabled (Kids already does). Cursor App
tokens cannot assign Copilot. Memory PR #24 is already on `main`. To start a
Copilot run: enable coding agent in repo Settings if needed, then open
https://github.com/copilot/agents (logged in as the operator), pick this
repo, and paste the brief. Or GitHub → issue #26 → assign Copilot.
